Party, it played a pivotal role in the 1917 October Revolution, which led to the establishment of the Soviet state. The CPSU governed the Soviet Union, a vast territory spanning Eastern Europe and Northern Asia, shaping global dynamics throughout the 20th century. Under the leadership of figures such as Vladimir Lenin, Joseph Stalin, and Leonid Brezhnev, the CPSU orchestrated significant socio-economic transformations and positioned the USSR as a superpower through its extensive influence on global communism.

